# Local first, live only after confirm

Do **not** deploy to production after finishing work.

## Required workflow

1. Make changes locally
2. Run / use the **local** admin + API and show the user how to check (e.g. `http://localhost:3210`)
3. Deploy live (Vercel `vercel --prod --yes`, Railway API, etc.) **only after the user explicitly confirms** — e.g. “live push”, “deploy live”, “confirm”, “ok live e dao”
4. Until they confirm, leave changes local / in the working tree
5. When they do confirm, deploy AgainERP admin (`erp.againerp.com`) from the repo root and tell them the live URL briefly after success
6. If the API also changed for that same confirm, deploy the Railway API when that workflow is already established in the session

## Forbidden

- Auto-deploying “so they can see it” without a clear live/confirm ask
- Treating “fix it” / “show me” as permission to deploy production

## Notes

- Prefer deploying the working tree that includes the fix (CLI upload), same as prior sessions
- Still do not force-push git, commit, or open PRs unless the user asks
